<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Bassa Cove</h1><p class="st-meta">1832 CE – 1839 CE · capital Bassa Cove</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A settlement for freed Black Americans on the Liberian coast, founded by Pennsylvania and New York colonisation societies on Quaker principles of peace and temperance.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the early 1830s the Young Men's Colonization Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> colonisation society, founded a settlement at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-john-river-liberia">St John</a> river, first called Port Cresson after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quakers">Quaker</a> colonisation advocate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elliott-cresson">Elliott Cresson</a>. Its settlers were free Black Americans and emancipated slaves.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony was run on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quakers">Quaker</a> principles: it forbade arms for aggression and banned the sale of alcohol, which also limited its trade with neighbours. In 1835 local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bassa-people-liberia">Bassa</a> forces, angered by the colony's opposition to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>, destroyed the settlement and killed many settlers. It was refounded as Bassa Cove, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-buchanan-governor">Thomas Buchanan</a> became its governor in 1836.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1839 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bassa-people-liberia">Bassa</a> Cove joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-liberia">Colony of Liberia</a> in the Commonwealth of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liberia">Liberia</a>, with Buchanan as governor of the whole. The town of Buchanan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-bassa-county">Grand Bassa County</a> stands near the site.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bassa-cove.jpg" alt="Bassa Cove" width="223" height="272"><figcaption>Image: Global Photographer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BuchananLiberia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1832 CE – 1839 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bassa Cove</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Thomas Buchanan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/liberia">Liberia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Port Cresson</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1836&amp;focus=bassa-cove" aria-label="Bassa Cove on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4402 1958 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bassa Cove lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4722 2214L4701 2198"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4701 2198h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4722 2214h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4722 2214h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1836&amp;focus=bassa-cove">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
